  "notes": "Higher weight = query first / trust faster. Cap 20. Min 1. Sweep on 2026-05-22 added 3 new sources, reweighted 14 existing. One new advisory: ClawHavoc — mass malicious-skill poisoning of OpenClaw's ClawHub marketplace (Koi, Feb 2026; 335+ skills drop Atomic Stealer via fake prerequisites; open-by-default marketplace). Three updates: axios compromise (added CVE-2026-34841 + named versions 1.14.1/0.30.4 + plain-crypto-js@4.2.1 RAT-dropper IOC + @usebruno/cli downstream, fixed 3.2.1), systemic MCP stdio class (added Atlassian mcp-atlassian MCPwnfluence CVE-2026-27825/-27826 unauth SSRF->arbitrary-write->RCE and Azure MCP Server missing-auth CVE-2026-32211), Comment-and-Control (added sibling Gemini CLI CVSS 10.0 --yolo/workspace-trust RCE, Novee+Pillar, fixed 0.39.1). New patterns this run: (1) AI-agent skill/plugin marketplace poisoning (ClawHub is npm/Open-VSX for OpenClaw skills; installing a skill == curl|bash; fake-prerequisite -> AMOS); (2) MCP servers as unauthenticated network services by default (mcp-atlassian/Azure/nginx-ui bind 0.0.0.0 with opt-in auth). Both folded into SKILL.md cautions + Tier-B rotation.",
